  "generated_text": "We can rewrite the system of equations as\n\\begin{align*}\nx + yz &= 7, \\\\\ny + xz &= 10, \\\\\nz + xy &= 10.\n\\end{align*}Adding all three equations, we get $x + y + z + yz + xz + xy = 27.$\n\nWe can factor the left-hand side as $(x + y + z)(1 + x + y + z) = 27.$\n\nSince $x + y + z \\neq 0,$ we can divide both sides by $x + y + z$ to get $1 + x + y + z = \\frac{27}{x + y + z}.$\n\nSubtracting 1 from both sides, we get $x + y + z = \\frac{27}{x + y + z} - 1.$\n\nSince $x + y + z \\neq 0,$ we can multiply both sides by $x + y + z$ to get $(x + y + z)^2 = 27 - (x + y + z).$\n\nTherefore, the answer is \\boxed{3}.The answer is: 3",
